SWEET AOC pre-load probe (patch 0161, plan 2026-11-14 oneshot-2 step A4), boot-arg sweetaoc=1. READS ONLY. Round 2 after run
o6-a4-aoc (phone hung before USB, no log): the PMU AOC power-domain status 0x17461884 bit 0 is read first (flexpmu_cal_local_gs101.h:3-20);
the GSA mailbox 0x17C90000 status/shared registers and the ACPM channel 13 descriptor in APM SRAM 0x02039000 are read always (stock: no
clock/power domain); aoc_req 0x175D0000 and the AOC SysMMU 0x1A090000 only when that bit is 1, else "skipped: pd off". The AOC S2MPU
0x1A0B0000 is never read. The probe runs in its own thread that starts once the USB log has sent a datagram (new counter
sweet_usblog_sent in sweet_usb.c, bounded 300 s) and prints "SWEET AOC PRE: aoc: reading <block>" 500 ms before each block, so a stall
names the block. Started from the top of sweet_trusty_init (patch 0156), the same hook point as sweetamp. Cites in bsd/dev/sweet_aoc.h
(host test shim/aoc_pre_host_test.c). Last line "SWEET AOC PRE: verdict PASS|FAIL reads=N pd=on|off". Without the boot-arg nothing changes.

